window.KNOWLEDGE = {"version":"Version 1 \u00b7 phone and tablet \u00b7 cell plugins 16.0.0-alpha","rules":"# Zapp mobile cell styles: rules\n\nVersion 1 \u00b7 phone and tablet \u00b7 cell plugins 16.0.0-alpha\n\nThese rules decide how a design becomes Zapp cell styles. They were learned by rebuilding a full streaming app\n(ITVX) cell by cell and reviewing the results on device. Follow them exactly: when a design asks for something\nthe rules say isn't possible, build the closest version and say what changed, why, and the alternative.\n\n## 1. The four cell types\n\n| Type | Use it for | Structure |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cell_1` | Tiles with text **below** the image (news tiles, thumbnails with titles under them) | Image on top, then up to 3 labels stacked below, optional buttons |\n| `cell_2` | Rows with the image **beside** the text (episode rows, list rows), and **text-only** cells (info blocks, action rows, channel rows) | Optional image on the left at a fixed width, up to 3 labels to its right, optional right-hand column (cell badge or action icon) |\n| `cell_3` | Text and buttons **over** the image (hero cards, posters with tags, detail heroes) | Full-width image; labels in one of three zones over it (top, centre, bottom), up to 3 per zone; optional buttons |\n| `cell_info` | Rail and list headers (\"Continue Watching\", \"View All\") | One title, an optional text button on the right |\n\nChoosing:\n- Text under a picture \u2192 `cell_1`. Text beside a picture, or no picture \u2192 `cell_2`. Text on a picture \u2192 `cell_3`.\n- A poster with a small tag on it (NEW, RECENTLY ADDED) \u2192 `cell_3` with the tag in the bottom zone.\n- A header row above a rail or list \u2192 `cell_info`.\n- If a `cell_3` design puts the text **below** the image (title, description and button under key art), it can\n  be built with bottom cell padding that reserves the space, but the text then can't grow; prefer `cell_1`\n  unless the design needs `cell_3`-only features.\n\n## 2. Text labels\n\n- **At most 3 labels** per cell (`cell_1`, `cell_2`), or 3 per zone (`cell_3`). Cell 2 has a 4th label in its\n  template but apps only render 3: never use it.\n- **One style per label**: one font, size, weight, colour and letter spacing. A line that mixes weights\n  (\"**Up next:** Lorraine\") or colours (\"06:00 \u00b7 <green>13m left<\/green>\") must use one style, or be split into\n  separate labels.\n- **No icons inside labels** (subtitles, guidance ratings, inline dots as images). Leave the icon out, or note\n  it as feed artwork.\n- Labels can have a **background colour, padding and a corner radius** (tags, pills). The radius applies to all\n  four corners or none: a tab with one rounded corner becomes square.\n- No gradient fills on text.\n- Per label: alignment (left, centre, right), number of lines (truncates with \u2026), uppercase transform, margins.\n- Each label reads a **data key**: `title`, `summary`, or any feed path such as `extensions.genre`.\n- When content needs more than 3 lines (e.g. an expanded live panel: logo, title, time, description, \"up next\"),\n  **split it across two cells** placed as two components that read the same feed. Record this as a\n  `workaround`.\n\n## 3. Images\n\n- One **main image** per cell, from a feed media key: `image_base` (landscape key art), `thumb_1` (title logo),\n  `thumb_2` (poster), `thumb_3` (still). Aspect ratio from presets (16x9, 4x3, 1x1, 3x4, 2x3, 9x16) or a custom\n  `WxH`. Corner radius, a border (width, colour) and a placeholder colour are available.\n- One **secondary image** (title logo, channel logo, rank artwork): fixed width and height, fitted inside that\n  box, positioned above or below a label or over the image. It has **no border** setting.\n- **Gradients and scrims** over the image are an **overlay image** (a PNG the studio generates from the gradient\n  stops). There is no gradient setting on the cell.\n- A design element that overlaps another (a rank number tucked behind a poster) can't be layered. Draw the\n  effect into artwork the feed supplies (e.g. one rank image per position, cropped so it looks tucked behind),\n  and place the pieces side by side. Record as `workaround`.\n- Promo banners, collection tiles and date strips that are part of the artwork are just images.\n\n## 4. Badges, pills and progress\n\n- **Duration / runtime pill**: always **bottom right** of the image (background, colour, font, radius, padding,\n  margins). A design with it elsewhere \u2192 keep bottom right and record the change; alternative: a content badge.\n- **Content badges** sit on the image (play buttons, LIVE pills, promo badges). A cell with no image can't show\n  them.\n- **Cell badge** (cell_2): an icon in the right-hand column (chevron, arrow) or on the image.\n- **Action icon** (cell_2): e.g. a download button in the right-hand column.\n- **Progress bar**: on top of the image, above or below text label 1 or 2, or at the bottom of the cell. Colour,\n  track colour, height, radius and margins. It **can't share a line with a label** (a bar with \"2m left\" at its\n  end): put the label on the line above (right-aligned) and give the bar a right margin to leave room. Extra\n  bottom margin only adds space under the cell.\n\n## 5. Buttons\n\n- Up to **3 buttons** per cell, stacked horizontally or vertically, aligned left or centre, positioned relative\n  to the labels or over the image.\n- Each button runs an **action plugin**: navigation (open / play), favourites (my list), share, downloads,\n  trailer.\n- **Labels and icons come from the action plugin**, set once for the whole app. The navigation action has one\n  label (e.g. \"Watch Now\"), so two navigation buttons with different labels (\"WATCH NOW\" + \"WATCH AD-FREE\",\n  or \"MORE INFO\") aren't possible: drop the second button, or note that it needs its own action plugin.\n  A \"MORE INFO\" button that opens the show reads the navigation label.\n- Icons come from the plugin's two flavours (light and dark): pick the flavour that suits the button colour.\n  A one-off icon colour (e.g. a lime icon on one button) isn't possible.\n- Per button: fill (full width), dynamic (fits its label) or a fixed width; background, text colour, border,\n  corner radius, padding, font; icon left, right or above the label.\n\n## 6. Layout, spacing and behaviour\n\n- Cell padding, background, corner radius and border (inside) are on the cell. Cell 2 also has top and bottom\n  **dividers** (thickness, colour, margins); they're inset by the cell's side padding. An edge-to-edge divider\n  with padded content isn't possible: accept the inset, or move side spacing to the component.\n- Cell 2 **centres its text vertically** against the image when the text is shorter than the image, and\n  top-aligns when taller. A full-width line under both the image and the text (e.g. a synopsis under an episode\n  row) isn't possible: the text stays beside the image.\n- Things around cells belong to the **component**, not the cell: carousel peek, page dots, rail gaps and item\n  widths, grid columns, side insets. Note them, don't build them.\n- **No expand/collapse**: cells can't open or close in place. Chevrons that toggle a row have no job: leave them\n  out and record why. Show an expanded state as its own cell(s).\n- A composition that depends on an exact width (number + poster) only works in a horizontal list with a fixed\n  item width.\n- Negative margins work but should be tested on device; prefer layouts that avoid them (e.g. swap which picture\n  is the main image).\n\n## 7. Reporting decisions\n\nFor every cell, record:\n- `works`: what carries over as designed.\n- `changed`: each visible difference, named (`item`), with the rule-based reason in plain words.\n- `alternative`: the suggested approach where there is one.\n\nStatus: `as_designed` (nothing material changed), `adapted` (visible changes), `workaround` (not possible\ndirectly; built another way).\n\nWrite decisions for a customer: plain language, no internal key names, one sentence each.\n","schema":"# Cell description format\n\nThe studio asks Claude to describe each distinct cell style in the supplied designs in this format. The studio's\nconverter turns each description into an importable Zapp cell style JSON, so describe what the platform will\nbuild (after applying the rules), not a perfect copy of the design. Anything that can't be built goes in\n`decisions`.\n\nAll sizes are in points at the device's width (phone 393, tablet 1133 unless told otherwise). Colours are\n`#rrggbb` or `rgba(r,g,b,a)`. Boxes are `[top, right, bottom, left]`.\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"cells\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Poster Tile\",                 // short, Title Case, unique per style\n      \"screen\": \"Home\",                       // where it appears\n      \"purpose\": \"Portrait poster for rails and grids, with an optional tag.\",\n      \"bbox\": { \"x\": 0.05, \"y\": 0.30, \"w\": 0.28, \"h\": 0.20 }, // one clear example in THIS image, fractions of the image (0-1)\n      \"plugin\": \"cell_3\",                     // cell_1 | cell_2 | cell_3 | cell_info  (see rules)\n      \"status\": \"as_designed\",                // as_designed | adapted | workaround\n      \"layout\": { \"type\": \"rail\", \"itemWidth\": 112, \"gap\": 8, \"padding\": 20 },\n      //   rail: horizontal list (itemWidth = the cell's width) \u00b7 list: vertical list (rowGap) \u00b7 single: one full-width cell\n      \"appBackground\": \"#172B3B\",             // the screen colour behind the cell\n      \"cell\": {\n        \"background\": \"rgba(0,0,0,0)\", \"radius\": 0, \"padding\": [0, 0, 0, 0],\n        \"border\": null,                       // or { \"width\": 1, \"color\": \"rgba(255,255,255,0.14)\" }\n        \"dividerTop\": null,                   // cell_2 only: { \"thickness\": 1, \"color\": \"#4B6F80\", \"margin\": [20, 0, 0, 0] }\n        \"dividerBottom\": null\n      },\n      \"image\": {                              // null when the cell has no picture (cell_2 and cell_info only)\n        \"key\": \"thumb_2\",                     // feed media key: image_base (landscape key art), thumb_1 (logo), thumb_2 (poster), thumb_3 (still)\n        \"ratio\": \"2x3\",                       // 16x9 | 4x3 | 1x1 | 3x4 | 2x3 | 9x16 | or any \"WxH\" (e.g. \"43x60\")\n        \"width\": 135,                         // cell_2 only: the image's width\n        \"radius\": 2,\n        \"border\": null,                       // or { \"width\": 1, \"color\": \"rgba(255,255,255,0.10)\" }\n        \"margin\": [0, 0, 0, 0],               // cell_1: bottom margin = gap to the text; cell_2: right margin = gap to the text\n        \"placeholder\": \"#203A4B\"\n      },\n      \"overlay\": null,                        // gradient over the image: { \"direction\": \"vertical\", \"stops\": [{ \"at\": 0, \"color\": \"rgba(0,0,0,0)\" }, { \"at\": 1, \"color\": \"rgba(10,22,30,0.92)\" }] }\n      \"secondaryImage\": null,                 // { \"key\": \"thumb_1\", \"width\": 240, \"height\": 56, \"align\": \"center\", \"beforeLabel\": 1, \"margin\": [0,16,12,16], \"fit\": \"center\" }\n                                              //   beforeLabel: index of the label it sits above (1-3); omit to sit below the last label; \"position\": \"over_image\" for over the picture\n      \"zone\": \"bottom\",                       // cell_3 only: where the text sits over the image: top | center | bottom\n      \"labels\": [                             // in reading order, max 3 (see rules)\n        {\n          \"role\": \"tag\",                      // short id: title, meta, tag, description...\n          \"dataKey\": \"extensions.tag\",        // title | summary | any feed path (extensions.genre, extensions.runtime)\n          \"sample\": \"RECENTLY ADDED\",         // the text in the design (used for the preview)\n          \"font\": { \"family\": \"DM Sans\", \"weight\": 500, \"size\": 9, \"lineHeight\": 12, \"letterSpacing\": 0.6 },\n          \"color\": \"#172B3B\",\n          \"background\": \"#E6F06E\",            // null for none\n          \"padding\": [1, 4, 1, 4], \"radius\": 2,\n          \"align\": \"center\",                  // left | center | right\n          \"lines\": 1,\n          \"uppercase\": true,\n          \"margin\": [0, 6, 5, 6]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"buttons\": null,                        // { \"stacking\": \"horizontal|vertical\", \"align\": \"left|center\", \"gap\": 8, \"margin\": [0,0,0,0], \"afterLabel\": 3 | \"position\": \"over_image\",\n                                              //   \"items\": [ { \"action\": \"navigation|favourites|share|downloads|trailer\", \"label\": true, \"icon\": true, \"iconPosition\": \"left|right|top\",\n                                              //               \"width\": \"fill\" | \"dynamic\" | 260, \"background\": \"#FFFFFF\", \"color\": \"#102C3D\", \"border\": null, \"radius\": 2,\n                                              //               \"padding\": [11,16,11,16], \"font\": {...}, \"iconSize\": 22, \"iconFlavour\": \"light|dark\" } ] }\n      \"progress\": null,                       // { \"position\": \"on_image | above_label_1 | below_label_1 | above_label_2 | below_label_2 | bottom_of_cell\",\n                                              //   \"height\": 4, \"color\": \"#A0FCBB\", \"track\": \"#2E4B5C\", \"radius\": 2, \"margin\": [6, 92, 0, 0] }\n      \"runtime\": null,                        // duration pill (always bottom right of the image): { \"background\": \"rgba(17,34,46,0.85)\", \"color\": \"#FFFFFF\", \"font\": {...}, \"radius\": 3, \"padding\": [1,5,1,5], \"margin\": [0,6,6,0] }\n      \"header\": null,                         // cell_info only: { \"title\": <label>, \"button\": { \"text\": \"View All\", \"font\": {...}, \"color\": \"#EBF66F\" } | null, \"padding\": [20, null, 12, null] }\n      \"decisions\": [                          // what works, what changed and why, and the suggested alternative\n        { \"type\": \"works\", \"text\": \"2:3 poster with a lime tag that hides when the feed has no tag.\" },\n        { \"type\": \"changed\", \"item\": \"Duration pill position\", \"text\": \"The runtime pill always sits bottom right; the design shows it top right.\" },\n        { \"type\": \"alternative\", \"text\": \"Use a content badge if the pill must be top right.\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nNotes for the describer:\n\n- One entry per distinct cell *style*. Ten posters in a rail are one Poster Tile.\n- Ignore the status bar, app navigation bar, tab bar and bottom tab bar: they aren't cells.\n- Fonts: give the family as designed (e.g. \"Inter\", \"DM Sans\", \"SF Pro Text\"). Weight as a number.\n- Measure in points: the studio tells you the image's pixel width and the screen width in points.\n- If the design needs more than the cell can do, build the closest version and record each difference as a\n  `changed` decision with the reason from the rules, plus an `alternative` where there is one.\n- `status`: `as_designed` when nothing material changed, `adapted` when something visible changed,\n  `workaround` when the design isn't possible directly and needed another approach (extra cell, feed artwork).\n","examples":{"note":"Worked examples from a reviewed build (a streaming app, phone, 393pt wide, dark slate theme). They show the expected detail and how decisions are written.","cells":[{"name":"Poster Tile","screen":"Home","purpose":"Portrait 2:3 poster for rails and grids, with an optional tag.","bbox":{"x":0.35,"y":0.24,"w":0.29,"h":0.2},"plugin":"cell_3","status":"as_designed","layout":{"type":"rail","itemWidth":112,"gap":8,"padding":20},"appBackground":"#172B3B","cell":{"background":"rgba(0,0,0,0)","radius":2,"padding":[0,0,0,0],"border":null},"image":{"key":"thumb_2","ratio":"2x3","radius":2,"border":null,"margin":[0,0,0,0],"placeholder":"#203A4B"},"overlay":null,"secondaryImage":null,"zone":"bottom","labels":[{"role":"tag","dataKey":"extensions.tag","sample":"RECENTLY ADDED","font":{"family":"DM Sans","weight":500,"size":9,"lineHeight":12,"letterSpacing":0.6},"color":"#172B3B","background":"#E6F06E","padding":[1,4,1,4],"radius":2,"align":"center","lines":1,"uppercase":true,"margin":[0,6,5,6]}],"buttons":null,"progress":null,"runtime":null,"decisions":[{"type":"works","text":"2:3 poster with the tag as a label with a background; it hides when the feed has no tag."},{"type":"works","text":"One style serves every rail and grid; the component sets the width."}]},{"name":"News Tile","screen":"Home","purpose":"News rail: 16:9 thumbnail with a duration pill, then a bold time-ago line and a headline.","bbox":{"x":0.04,"y":0.51,"w":0.48,"h":0.17},"plugin":"cell_1","status":"adapted","layout":{"type":"rail","itemWidth":172,"gap":8,"padding":20},"appBackground":"#172B3B","cell":{"background":"rgba(0,0,0,0)","radius":0,"padding":[0,0,0,0],"border":null},"image":{"key":"image_base","ratio":"16x9","radius":2,"border":null,"margin":[0,0,10,0],"placeholder":"#203A4B"},"overlay":null,"secondaryImage":null,"labels":[{"role":"time","dataKey":"extensions.published","sample":"1 hour ago","font":{"family":"DM Sans","weight":700,"size":14,"lineHeight":19,"letterSpacing":0},"color":"#FFFFFF","background":null,"padding":[0,0,0,0],"radius":0,"align":"left","lines":1,"uppercase":false,"margin":[0,0,0,0]},{"role":"headline","dataKey":"title","sample":"The latest headlines as the Duchess of Sussex pulls out of a speech","font":{"family":"DM Sans","weight":400,"size":14,"lineHeight":19,"letterSpacing":0},"color":"#FFFFFF","background":null,"padding":[0,0,0,0],"radius":0,"align":"left","lines":3,"uppercase":false,"margin":[0,0,0,0]}],"buttons":null,"progress":null,"runtime":{"background":"rgba(17,34,46,0.85)","color":"#FFFFFF","font":{"family":"DM Sans","weight":500,"size":11,"lineHeight":14,"letterSpacing":0},"radius":3,"padding":[1,5,1,5],"margin":[0,6,6,0]},"decisions":[{"type":"works","text":"16:9 thumbnail with a styled duration pill, a time-ago line and a 3-line headline."},{"type":"changed","item":"Duration pill position","text":"The runtime pill always sits bottom right; the design shows it top right."},{"type":"changed","item":"Two labels, not one line","text":"The bold time and regular headline run on in one line in the design; a label has one weight, so they are two labels."},{"type":"alternative","text":"Use a content badge if the pill must be top right."}]},{"name":"Live Channel Row","screen":"Live","purpose":"Collapsed channel row: channel logo, the programme on now, a progress bar and the time left.","bbox":{"x":0.0,"y":0.39,"w":1.0,"h":0.11},"plugin":"cell_2","status":"adapted","layout":{"type":"list","rowGap":0,"padding":0},"appBackground":"#172B3B","cell":{"background":"#172B3B","radius":0,"padding":[20,20,0,20],"border":null,"dividerTop":null,"dividerBottom":{"thickness":1,"color":"#4B6F80","margin":[20,0,0,0]}},"image":null,"overlay":null,"secondaryImage":{"key":"thumb_1","width":80,"height":18,"align":"left","beforeLabel":1,"margin":[0,0,16,0],"fit":"bottom_left"},"labels":[{"role":"title","dataKey":"title","sample":"The Real Housewives Of Rhode Island (S1)","font":{"family":"DM Sans","weight":400,"size":15,"lineHeight":19,"letterSpacing":0},"color":"#FFFFFF","background":null,"padding":[0,0,0,0],"radius":0,"align":"left","lines":1,"uppercase":false,"margin":[0,0,8,0]},{"role":"time-left","dataKey":"extensions.time-left","sample":"2m left","font":{"family":"DM Sans","weight":700,"size":15,"lineHeight":19,"letterSpacing":0},"color":"#A0FCBB","background":null,"padding":[0,0,0,0],"radius":0,"align":"right","lines":1,"uppercase":false,"margin":[0,0,0,0]}],"buttons":null,"progress":{"position":"bottom_of_cell","height":4,"color":"#A0FCBB","track":"#2E4B5C","radius":2,"margin":[6,92,0,0]},"runtime":null,"decisions":[{"type":"works","text":"Channel logo, programme title and time left, with the progress bar at the bottom of the cell."},{"type":"changed","item":"Time left above the bar","text":"A label and the progress bar can't share a line, so \"2m left\" is right-aligned on the line above and the bar leaves room on the right."},{"type":"changed","item":"No expand/collapse chevron","text":"Cells can't expand or collapse, so the chevron would do nothing."},{"type":"alternative","text":"The feed needs to supply progress for the programme on now."}]},{"name":"Section Header","screen":"Home","purpose":"Rail header: bold title and a View All link.","bbox":{"x":0.0,"y":0.19,"w":1.0,"h":0.045},"plugin":"cell_info","status":"as_designed","layout":{"type":"single","padding":0},"appBackground":"#172B3B","cell":{"background":"rgba(0,0,0,0)","radius":0,"padding":[20,20,12,20],"border":null},"image":null,"labels":[],"header":{"title":{"role":"title","dataKey":"title","sample":"Our Top Picks","font":{"family":"DM Sans","weight":700,"size":18,"lineHeight":23,"letterSpacing":-0.2},"color":"#FFFFFF","align":"left","lines":1,"uppercase":false},"button":{"text":"View All","font":{"family":"DM Sans","weight":500,"size":16,"lineHeight":20,"letterSpacing":0},"color":"#EBF66F"}},"decisions":[{"type":"works","text":"Feed title as the header, with View All as a text-only header button."}]}]}};
